# Vexa — review ownership.
#
# The LAST matching rule wins, so the global fallback must stay at the top:
# every rule below it overrides it. Moving `*` to the bottom would make the
# Team Lead the only reviewer for the whole repository.
#
# GitHub excludes the PR author from its own reviewer list. That is why every
# path has at least two owners — otherwise an owner's PR gets no reviewer and
# hangs forever. The only exception is /.github/, see the note at the bottom.

# Global fallback — Team Lead reviews everything by default
*                       @terekh373

# Backend: Team Lead + backend dev
/backend/               @terekh373 @suberbobbr

# Database contract: schema, migrations, seed. Changing it out of band breaks
# integration between backend and both clients.
/backend/prisma/        @terekh373 @suberbobbr
/docs/schema.dbml       @terekh373 @suberbobbr

# Frontend web + mobile: both frontend devs review each other
/web/                   @devitfro @voer2
/mobile/                @devitfro @voer2

# Project documentation
/docs/                  @terekh373

# Infra: Team Lead only. A PR here cannot be approved by anyone else, so the
# Team Lead merges it by temporarily disabling the protect-develop ruleset.
/.github/               @terekh373
